# L §3.2 Differences, Key arithmetic; §8.4 R-load (tally 2.1.7, R5, issue #144, the builder's SR-B2, pick P40): key
# arithmetic past a list index (kq + 1 at its last key) stands in a value position here, the difference of two keys,
# which is the difference of their positions; a result outside the index has none, so the difference has no meaning
# for its values: RUN-DOMAIN at the value, in the operands' words (as `0.1 + q1` is), the run going on. refcore 2.1.6
# crashed there (REFCORE-NOT-YET, TypeError). Either side, and against a key input.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
index qs = [q1, q2]
input kq: key qs
input kp: key qs
def z1: int = q1 - (kq + 1)
def z2: int = (kq + 1) - kp
def z3: int = kq - kp

ask a1: z1
ask a2: z2
ask a3: z3

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  kq = q2
  kp = q1
=== expect
a1: refused: RUN-DOMAIN q1 - q2 + 1
  cut 2026-03-01
a2: refused: RUN-DOMAIN q2 + 1 - q1
  cut 2026-03-01
a3: 1
  cut 2026-03-01
